  "result": "Fixed in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. It uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as a comment start by default, so anything from a `#` onward was dropped before completion ran. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is kept as an ordinary character.\n\n`split_arg_string('cmd a#b #c')` now returns `['cmd', 'a#b', '#c']`, and the shell completion tests pass (58 passed). I didn't add a regression test and haven't committed anything.",
